/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 60 0 R
/T ( This study adheres to UK ethical standards for qualitative & lived experience research, including respect for autonomy, dignity, confidentiality & informed consent. All treatments, cultural practices, and hospital admissions described were voluntary and initiated by the participant as part of an informed self management & safety strategy. No compulsory or coercive interventions were used. Informed consent was obtained and revisited throughout the research process. Identifying information relating to family members and children has been anonymised. No clinical records were accessed; all data derive from first person narrative and reflective documentation.)
/E ( This study adheres to UK ethical standards for qualitative & lived experience research, including respect for autonomy, dignity, confidentiality & informed consent. All treatments, cultural practices, and hospital admissions described were voluntary and initiated by the participant as part of an informed self management & safety strategy. No compulsory or coercive interventions were used. Informed consent was obtained and revisited throughout the research process. Identifying information relating to family members and children has been anonymised. No clinical records were accessed; all data derive from first person narrative and reflective documentation.)
